621	f027d23f-f32f-4c7a-9963-47647963b752	other	Good evening, and welcome to The Briton Brief. Tonight—a seismic shift in British defence strategy. Has the sun finally set on the so-called "Special Relationship"?\n\nIn a stark and unprecedented warning, Lord George Robertson—the former head of NATO and a chief architect of the Government's Strategic Defence Review—has declared that Britain's military reliance on the United States is, quote, "no longer tenable."\n\nSpeaking at Chatham House, Lord Robertson shattered a decades-old Whitehall consensus. He warned that a naïve belief that Washington will "always be there" has severely diminished our own armed forces. Crucially, he stressed that this is a permanent geopolitical fracture. Driven by a pivot towards China and a deep scepticism of globalisation, American foreign policy is becoming strictly transactional—regardless of whether Donald Trump, or anyone else, occupies the Oval Office.\n\nThis dramatic intervention comes at a moment of severe transatlantic strain. Prime Minister Sir Keir Starmer recently defied Mr Trump’s aggressive demands for Britain to join his escalating war in Iran. In retaliation, the US President has repeatedly undermined NATO—branding the historic alliance a "paper tiger"—and stoked fury by threatening to seize control of Greenland.\n\nLord Robertson is not a lone voice in the wilderness. The Lords International Relations and Defence Committee has urged ministers to permanently banish the "sentimental illusion" of an unbreakable transatlantic bond. Peers are now demanding a radical rebalancing—urging Downing Street to deepen military ties with our European neighbours as a vital hedge against an increasingly unpredictable ally.\n\nIn a hasty attempt at diplomatic damage control, the US Ambassador to London, Warren Stephens, insisted today that the UK remains America’s closest partner, citing a shared commitment to European security. But behind closed doors in Westminster, the harsh reality is setting in: Britain must urgently learn to stand on its own two feet.\n\nStay subscribed to The Briton Brief, as we track this monumental turning point in British military history.	fable		fable	1	mp3	2613fb42-c9f9-46f0-8c53-607f57f400ba	COMPLETED	/app/media/audio_files/26344687-23cb-40fe-b877-f0c805c4d90f_f027d23f-f32f-4c7a-9963-47647963b752.mp3		1814	2026-04-23 14:57:15.202456+00	2026-04-23 14:57:42.383728+00	26344687-23cb-40fe-b877-f0c805c4d90f
