994	f078b34d-9e97-4fad-9543-c41eb8c9e882	other	A thunderous noise does not always signify strength... occasionally, it is merely a hollow void. A famished fox prowled through a shadowy wood when a dreadful, booming sound rattled the branches. Advancing with caution, he discovered a colossal drum suspended from a tree, beaten by the fierce wind. His mouth watered, assuming a beast of such magnitude must be brimming with flesh and fat. He pounced, viciously tearing the drum apart. The revelation? Nothing at all. Merely barren wood and hide. A total waste of his cunning. The moral: The most imposing figures and the loudest voices often conceal an absolute emptiness. Do not be deceived by grand appearances; true worth lies in substance, not empty clamour.	fable		fable	1	mp3	943757b7-fdb4-4c38-8718-7410098f1ead	COMPLETED	/app/media/audio_files/26344687-23cb-40fe-b877-f0c805c4d90f_f078b34d-9e97-4fad-9543-c41eb8c9e882.mp3		598	2026-04-25 17:20:39.569574+00	2026-04-25 17:20:50.441669+00	26344687-23cb-40fe-b877-f0c805c4d90f
